<title>PAKISTAN: 150 T vegoil destroyed in Pakistan tankers dispute.</title>
<headline>150 T vegoil destroyed in Pakistan tankers dispute.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>At least 150 tonnes of palm oil and soyoil were spilled by supporters of the Tankers Owners Association, who are on strike to press their demand for a rise in freight charges, dealers said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;At least 150 tonnes of vegetable oils have been spilled by the strikers at Nooriabad near Karachi on Monday,&quot; dealer Kamran Khan of Saulat Enterprises said.</p>
<p>The valves of at least eight tankers, each carrying 22 tonnes of oil, were forcibly opened, he said.</p>
<p>The oil was worth 4.8 million rupees ($119,000), dealers said.</p>
